WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.534 --> 00:00:04.534
-As Republicans salivate over
the discovery of a small number

00:00:04.534 --> 00:00:06.601
of classified documents
in Joe Biden's home

00:00:06.601 --> 00:00:07.634
and private office,

00:00:07.634 --> 00:00:09.100
Donald Trump's
many criminal probes

00:00:09.100 --> 00:00:11.267
are intensifying,
and Trump is freaking out.

00:00:11.267 --> 00:00:13.467
In response, he called in
to a right-wing radio show

00:00:13.467 --> 00:00:15.934
and called the special counsel
investigating him

00:00:15.934 --> 00:00:17.133
a terrorist.

00:00:17.133 --> 00:00:18.734
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:18.734 --> 00:00:20.267
[ Theme music plays ]

00:00:20.267 --> 00:00:23.033
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:23.033 --> 00:00:26.367
Going into last year's midterms,
House Speaker Kevin McCarthy

00:00:26.367 --> 00:00:28.868
and his fellow Republicans were
expecting a landslide victory

00:00:28.868 --> 00:00:31.367
that would give them a large
majority in the House

00:00:31.367 --> 00:00:33.734
and a mandate to go on offense
against Joe Biden

00:00:33.734 --> 00:00:35.701
and the Democrats.
In fact, for at least a year

00:00:35.701 --> 00:00:37.834
leading up to the midterms,
McCarthy was incredibly cocky

00:00:37.834 --> 00:00:39.767
about it, even giving out
specific numbers

00:00:39.767 --> 00:00:41.701
for how many seats Republican
could win.

00:00:41.701 --> 00:00:45.934
-It could be one of the biggest
election losses for Democrats.

00:00:45.934 --> 00:00:48.601
I think anywhere over 20
is a red wave.

00:00:48.601 --> 00:00:51.467
We want to earn enough that
we have a governing majority.

00:00:51.467 --> 00:00:53.701
That means getting in the realm
of 20 and higher.

00:00:53.701 --> 00:00:56.767
If we were fortunate enough
to win 35 Republican seats,

00:00:56.767 --> 00:00:59.667
that would be the largest
Republican majority

00:00:59.667 --> 00:01:01.400
in more than 100 years.

00:01:01.400 --> 00:01:04.133
There's about 55 to 70 seats
that we can play in

00:01:04.133 --> 00:01:05.601
and make them competitive.

00:01:05.601 --> 00:01:08.167
-Is there any chance Republicans
are a little overconfident

00:01:08.167 --> 00:01:11.968
this year?
-No, we're not overconfident.

00:01:11.968 --> 00:01:14.767
-"There's gonna be historic
red wave or my name's not

00:01:14.767 --> 00:01:16.901
Klevin McCorthy.
[Bleep] Hold on!"

00:01:16.901 --> 00:01:19.834
[ Laughter ]

00:01:19.834 --> 00:01:21.667
It's never a good sign
when someone says

00:01:21.667 --> 00:01:23.234
they're not being
overconfident.

00:01:23.234 --> 00:01:25.634
If a character says that in
a movie, he's about 10 minutes

00:01:25.634 --> 00:01:27.634
away from getting eaten
by a T-Rex.

00:01:27.634 --> 00:01:30.033
"I'm not overconfident!
I'm your only way

00:01:30.033 --> 00:01:32.467
out of this park!
[ Screams ]"

00:01:32.467 --> 00:01:34.367
[ Laughter ]

00:01:34.367 --> 00:01:36.400
McCarthy was so overconfident,
he was even predicting

00:01:36.400 --> 00:01:39.200
the safe blue seats where Biden
beat Trump by double digits

00:01:39.200 --> 00:01:40.968
would be vulnerable to
Republicans, and he warned

00:01:40.968 --> 00:01:42.767
the members of Congress
in those seats

00:01:42.767 --> 00:01:44.267
that they could soon be
out of jobs.

00:01:44.267 --> 00:01:47.334
-If you're a Democrat,
and President Biden

00:01:47.334 --> 00:01:50.100
won your seat by 16 points,

00:01:50.100 --> 00:01:52.033
you're in a competitive race
next year.

00:01:52.033 --> 00:01:53.534
You are no longer safe.

00:01:53.534 --> 00:01:56.501
-"You are no longer safe"?
Are you a member of Congress

00:01:56.501 --> 00:01:58.734
or a stalker ex-husband
from a Lifetime movie

00:01:58.734 --> 00:02:00.667
called "Taking back the House?"

00:02:00.667 --> 00:02:04.167
[ Laughter ]

00:02:04.167 --> 00:02:05.634
"Kevin!
What are you doing here?!

00:02:05.634 --> 00:02:07.000
You don't live here anymore!"

00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:08.968
"I helped pay for this house,
Carol, and if you think

00:02:08.968 --> 00:02:11.868
I'm gonna stand by while you
turn into the town harlot,

00:02:11.868 --> 00:02:14.133
you are sadly mistaken!
You are no longer safe!"

00:02:14.133 --> 00:02:15.534
[ Laughter ]

00:02:15.534 --> 00:02:17.801
Anyway, the point is, McCarthy
was confidently predicting

00:02:17.801 --> 00:02:19.868
enough seats for what he called
a governing majority,

00:02:19.868 --> 00:02:21.968
meaning majority big enough
that he could get stuff done

00:02:21.968 --> 00:02:24.968
without having to beg and plead
with every individual member

00:02:24.968 --> 00:02:27.000
of his caucus.
As we all know now,

00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:28.834
that did not happen,
and McCarthy had to concede

00:02:28.834 --> 00:02:31.567
to virtually anything
anyone wanted from him

00:02:31.567 --> 00:02:32.801
to get their vote.
For example,

00:02:32.801 --> 00:02:35.234
allowing just one Republican
to call for a vote

00:02:35.234 --> 00:02:37.200
to remove him as Speaker
at any time -- one member.

00:02:37.200 --> 00:02:39.868
That means any time
Lauren Boebert has a bad day,

00:02:39.868 --> 00:02:41.267
she can take it out on
Kevin McCarthy,

00:02:41.267 --> 00:02:44.300
which is a problem because
she only has bad days.

00:02:44.300 --> 00:02:45.767
Don't get me wrong --
she loves bad days.

00:02:45.767 --> 00:02:47.634
She's built for bad days.
She's the only person

00:02:47.634 --> 00:02:49.801
who wears a T-shirt that says,
"Thank God it's Monday."

00:02:49.801 --> 00:02:51.133
[ Laughter ]

00:02:51.133 --> 00:02:53.133
Anyway, the point is,
McCarthy had to beg and plead

00:02:53.133 --> 00:02:54.868
to get his job,
and for help with that,

00:02:54.868 --> 00:02:57.067
he turned to Donald Trump.
Now, as we've explained before,

00:02:57.067 --> 00:02:59.200
Trump is actually a big reason
McCarthy has

00:02:59.200 --> 00:03:00.834
such a small majority
in the first place.

00:03:00.834 --> 00:03:03.901
Instead of staying out
of the primary process,

00:03:03.901 --> 00:03:06.367
and letting more conventional
GOP candidates

00:03:06.367 --> 00:03:08.367
win their races,
Trump kept endorsing

00:03:08.367 --> 00:03:09.968
his collection of MAGA goons.

00:03:09.968 --> 00:03:11.767
McCarthy would say,
"Here's a good choice.

00:03:11.767 --> 00:03:14.267
He's pro-military
and anti-taxes."

00:03:14.267 --> 00:03:16.300
And then Trump would say,
"I also have a guy.

00:03:16.300 --> 00:03:18.534
He's for sure a pyromaniac..."

00:03:18.534 --> 00:03:19.767
[ Laughter ]

00:03:19.767 --> 00:03:21.701
"...and he once punched a horse
at a county fair,

00:03:21.701 --> 00:03:23.834
but he also has my name tattooed
on his forehead,

00:03:23.834 --> 00:03:25.100
so he's a sharp guy."

00:03:25.100 --> 00:03:26.400
[ Laughter ]

00:03:26.400 --> 00:03:28.200
If it wasn't for Trump-endorsed
candidates failing

00:03:28.200 --> 00:03:30.300
in the general election,
Republicans probably would have

00:03:30.300 --> 00:03:32.434
won a lot more seats,
and McCarthy would have breezed

00:03:32.434 --> 00:03:34.701
through the Speaker vote.
Instead, Trump tanked the party,

00:03:34.701 --> 00:03:37.868
and McCarthy's razor-thin margin
relies on Trump fanatics.

00:03:37.868 --> 00:03:39.934
So to get them on board,
McCarthy had to rely on

00:03:39.934 --> 00:03:41.734
Trump's help,
which he openly admitted.

00:03:41.734 --> 00:03:45.534
-I do want to especially thank
President Trump.

00:03:45.534 --> 00:03:47.801
I don't think he should --
anybody should doubt

00:03:47.801 --> 00:03:49.434
his influence.

00:03:49.434 --> 00:03:51.234
He was with me
from the beginning.

00:03:51.234 --> 00:03:53.767
Somebody wrote the doubt
is why he was there,

00:03:53.767 --> 00:03:55.200
and he was all in.

00:03:55.200 --> 00:03:56.934
And he was a great influence
to make that all happen,

00:03:56.934 --> 00:03:58.767
so thank you, President Trump.

00:03:58.767 --> 00:04:01.534
-As a general rule, it's weird
to publicly thank someone

00:04:01.534 --> 00:04:04.200
who is under multiple
criminal investigations.

00:04:04.200 --> 00:04:06.133
During her Golden Globes speech,
Jennifer Coolidge

00:04:06.133 --> 00:04:09.534
didn't thank the actual Italian
Mafia, although in her case,

00:04:09.534 --> 00:04:10.934
I don't think she should
thank anyone.

00:04:10.934 --> 00:04:12.100
She's Jennifer Coolidge.

00:04:12.100 --> 00:04:14.167
She should give
a "you're welcome" speech.

00:04:14.167 --> 00:04:15.868
[ Cheers and applause ]
Yeah.

00:04:15.868 --> 00:04:18.133
She should just get up there,
take her award,

00:04:18.133 --> 00:04:20.567
say, "Wow!"
And then just walk off.

00:04:20.567 --> 00:04:23.334
[ Laughter ]

00:04:23.334 --> 00:04:25.567
But the last person you should
be thanking is Trump.

00:04:25.567 --> 00:04:26.701
That's the point at which
McCarthy

00:04:26.701 --> 00:04:27.968
should have been played off.

00:04:27.968 --> 00:04:30.567
-I do want to especially
thank, uh, President Trump.

00:04:30.567 --> 00:04:32.234
[ Fanfare plays loudly ]

00:04:32.234 --> 00:04:33.968
I don't think...

00:04:33.968 --> 00:04:35.667
-Of course,
this year's Golden Globe

00:04:35.667 --> 00:04:38.067
had that haunting piano --
the same haunting piano

00:04:38.067 --> 00:04:39.868
that plays in
"Taking Back the House"

00:04:39.868 --> 00:04:41.701
when Kevin emerges
from behind the curtain.

00:04:41.701 --> 00:04:44.367
[ Haunting piano music plays ]

00:04:44.367 --> 00:04:45.801
[ Laughter ]

00:04:45.801 --> 00:04:47.200
The point is,
the Speaker of the House

00:04:47.200 --> 00:04:49.334
is now publicly indebted
to a guy who openly plotted

00:04:49.334 --> 00:04:50.901
a coup against
the United States government.

00:04:50.901 --> 00:04:53.100
In fact, the multiple
criminal investigations

00:04:53.100 --> 00:04:54.434
into Trump are now intensifying.

00:04:54.434 --> 00:04:56.701
On Friday, for example,
Trump's family company

00:04:56.701 --> 00:05:00.667
was hit with the maximum fine
allowed under New York State law

00:05:00.667 --> 00:05:03.200
for running a years-long
tax fraud scheme.

00:05:03.200 --> 00:05:04.868
-Tonight the Trump Organization
has been hit

00:05:04.868 --> 00:05:07.901
with the maximum penalty --
$1.6 million --

00:05:07.901 --> 00:05:10.167
after being found guilty
of a years-long scheme

00:05:10.167 --> 00:05:12.834
to pay top executives
with cars, apartments,

00:05:12.834 --> 00:05:15.501
and school tuition,
all to avoid paying tax.

00:05:15.501 --> 00:05:17.300
-No, I think it's great
that Trump's company

00:05:17.300 --> 00:05:18.567
was held criminally accountable.

00:05:18.567 --> 00:05:21.601
But only $1.6 million?

00:05:21.601 --> 00:05:24.100
Trump probably
keeps that much change

00:05:24.100 --> 00:05:26.334
in his big-ass coat.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:26.334 --> 00:05:27.634
I mean, look.
He looks like he should be

00:05:27.634 --> 00:05:29.701
standing in line
at a Coinstar machine.

00:05:29.701 --> 00:05:31.667
Trump's company got
the maximum fine

00:05:31.667 --> 00:05:33.701
from a criminal tax-fraud
conviction.

00:05:33.701 --> 00:05:36.267
Then, we found out last week
that the Justice Department

00:05:36.267 --> 00:05:38.100
has issued yet another
flurry of subpoenas

00:05:38.100 --> 00:05:40.334
to Trump officials
as part of their investigation

00:05:40.334 --> 00:05:42.000
into the coup attempt
on January 6th.

00:05:42.000 --> 00:05:43.901
-We are keeping a new eye
on some new moves

00:05:43.901 --> 00:05:45.801
in that DOJ
criminal investigation

00:05:45.801 --> 00:05:48.200
into January 6th,
with the Washington Post

00:05:48.200 --> 00:05:51.300
now reporting on its new
and wide-ranging subpoena

00:05:51.300 --> 00:05:54.300
that the Justice Department sent
to Trump campaign officials.

00:05:54.300 --> 00:05:56.701
It asks some new questions
related to the 6th,

00:05:56.701 --> 00:05:58.400
according to The Post,
for information

00:05:58.400 --> 00:06:00.701
about stuff like
what these people said

00:06:00.701 --> 00:06:02.667
about voting machines
after 2020;

00:06:02.667 --> 00:06:05.334
for documents about
the fundraising and planning

00:06:05.334 --> 00:06:06.534
that went into
then-President Trump's

00:06:06.534 --> 00:06:07.701
rally on the 6th.

00:06:07.701 --> 00:06:08.968
-Now, this is big,

00:06:08.968 --> 00:06:10.567
because you know
what the punishment is

00:06:10.567 --> 00:06:11.701
for instigating a coup.

00:06:11.701 --> 00:06:13.701
[ Dramatic music plays ]

00:06:13.701 --> 00:06:16.501
-One million dollars.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:16.501 --> 00:06:18.000
-Big-time stuff.

00:06:18.000 --> 00:06:20.200
But more subpoenas
are going out.

00:06:20.200 --> 00:06:22.367
For example, prosecutors
have subpoenaed Mike Pence

00:06:22.367 --> 00:06:25.167
to find out what the [Bleep]
is going on with this run.

00:06:25.167 --> 00:06:28.167
[ Laughter ]

00:06:28.167 --> 00:06:31.100
The Justice Department needs to
get to the bottom of that.

00:06:31.100 --> 00:06:35.033
The only time it makes sense
to run and clap at the same time

00:06:35.033 --> 00:06:38.434
is if your dog is humping
a stranger's leg in the park.

00:06:38.434 --> 00:06:40.934
"Atlas, no! No!

00:06:40.934 --> 00:06:43.734
Atlas, no humping!
We discussed this!"

00:06:43.734 --> 00:06:45.934
[ Laughter ]

00:06:45.934 --> 00:06:47.267
And we played this clip
last week,

00:06:47.267 --> 00:06:48.801
and somehow
it was the first time

00:06:48.801 --> 00:06:50.701
I and a lot of our viewers
had seen it.

00:06:50.701 --> 00:06:52.067
And it only
raised more questions.

00:06:52.067 --> 00:06:53.601
I mean, look at
the rhythm of his clapping.

00:06:53.601 --> 00:06:55.300
He's...
[ Laughter ]

00:06:55.300 --> 00:06:57.667
...like the weirdest metronome
I've ever seen.

00:06:57.667 --> 00:07:01.234
He's like a -- like a T-1000
that got reprogrammed.

00:07:01.234 --> 00:07:02.567
[ Laughter ]

00:07:02.567 --> 00:07:04.934
And there may be new areas
of investigative interest,

00:07:04.934 --> 00:07:07.534
but it's a lot of the old names.
For example, prosecutors

00:07:07.534 --> 00:07:09.601
are focused yet again
on a close Trump ally

00:07:09.601 --> 00:07:11.567
who has been in and out
of legal trouble,

00:07:11.567 --> 00:07:13.901
basically nonstop,
for several years now.

00:07:13.901 --> 00:07:15.767
-Former Trump attorney
Rudy Giuliani

00:07:15.767 --> 00:07:17.534
has been subpoenaed
for documents

00:07:17.534 --> 00:07:20.300
related to payments he received
around the 2020 election.

00:07:20.300 --> 00:07:22.267
A source tells CNN
the subpoena is

00:07:22.267 --> 00:07:24.300
part of Special Counsel
Jack Smith's

00:07:24.300 --> 00:07:27.901
sweeping criminal probe into
Trump's fundraising and spending

00:07:27.901 --> 00:07:30.367
as he tried to overturn
the 2020 election.

00:07:30.367 --> 00:07:32.000
That's right,
Rudy was subpoenaed.

00:07:32.000 --> 00:07:34.167
I bet I know what face he made
when he found out.

00:07:34.167 --> 00:07:35.734
Ooh. I tricked you.

00:07:35.734 --> 00:07:37.133
You guys thought
I was gonna show

00:07:37.133 --> 00:07:39.000
the one where his eyes
are bugging out of his head.

00:07:39.000 --> 00:07:40.300
[ Laughter ]

00:07:40.300 --> 00:07:43.067
No, that's not how Rudy
would react to a subpoena.

00:07:43.067 --> 00:07:45.734
That's how he'd react
to seeing Mike Pence run.

00:07:45.734 --> 00:07:46.968
[ Laughter ]

00:07:46.968 --> 00:07:49.234
Mike Pence runs like
one of those ball thingies

00:07:49.234 --> 00:07:52.367
bosses have in movies
on their desk.

00:07:52.367 --> 00:07:53.701
[ Laughter ]

00:07:53.701 --> 00:07:55.100
It won't surprise you to learn

00:07:55.100 --> 00:07:56.934
that all this has made Trump
very unhappy.

00:07:56.934 --> 00:07:59.334
Last week, he called in
to a right-wing radio show

00:07:59.334 --> 00:08:01.968
and threw a hissy fit
about the special counsel

00:08:01.968 --> 00:08:04.767
who's investigating him --
a guy named Jack Smith.

00:08:28.601 --> 00:08:30.667
-Hey! First of all,

00:08:30.667 --> 00:08:32.467
no one should be
held responsible

00:08:32.467 --> 00:08:34.200
for what
their wife's sister does,

00:08:34.200 --> 00:08:36.734
my man!
[ Laughter ]

00:08:36.734 --> 00:08:38.934
That's not cool!

00:08:38.934 --> 00:08:41.000
Bad enough you got to
spend all day worrying

00:08:41.000 --> 00:08:42.901
what your wife's doing
behind your back.

00:08:42.901 --> 00:08:44.367
But her sister?

00:08:44.367 --> 00:08:46.000
[Bleep] you, dude.

00:08:46.000 --> 00:08:47.367
[ Laughter ]

00:08:47.367 --> 00:08:51.033
Also, how does Trump even have
all of this information

00:08:51.033 --> 00:08:52.534
about a guy's extended family?

00:08:52.534 --> 00:08:55.734
Is he just sitting down
with ancestry.com every night,

00:08:55.734 --> 00:08:57.634
looking for new enemies?

00:08:57.634 --> 00:08:59.400
"I just got a hint leaf,

00:08:59.400 --> 00:09:01.400
and it says that his wife
has a sister

00:09:01.400 --> 00:09:04.033
who does not like
Trump or cilantro."

00:09:04.033 --> 00:09:05.734
[ Laughter ]

00:09:05.734 --> 00:09:07.734
This is, yet again,
one of the many differences

00:09:07.734 --> 00:09:10.300
between the situations Trump and
Biden find themselves in.

00:09:10.300 --> 00:09:13.334
Trump is under multiple separate
criminal investigations.

00:09:13.334 --> 00:09:14.801
He's lied about them
at every turn,

00:09:14.801 --> 00:09:16.901
refused to cooperate,
obstructed the investigations,

00:09:16.901 --> 00:09:20.334
and is now calling the
prosecutor investigating him

00:09:20.334 --> 00:09:22.567
a terrorist.
Biden is at least cooperating.

00:09:22.567 --> 00:09:24.367
The worst thing you could say
about Biden is,

00:09:24.367 --> 00:09:27.334
there was no reason for him
to keep classified documents

00:09:27.334 --> 00:09:29.667
in the garage where
he also parks his Corvette.

00:09:29.667 --> 00:09:31.167
-According to
President Joe Biden,

00:09:31.167 --> 00:09:34.501
these classified documents were
found in his personal library

00:09:34.501 --> 00:09:37.501
and in the garage of his home
in Wilmington, Delaware.

00:09:37.501 --> 00:09:39.000
Just moments ago,

00:09:39.000 --> 00:09:41.267
Biden addressed the matter
very briefly, saying

00:09:41.267 --> 00:09:44.934
it was a locked garage where
he also keeps his Corvette.

00:09:44.934 --> 00:09:47.634
-Let me -- I'm gonna get
a chance to speak

00:09:47.634 --> 00:09:49.234
on all of this, God willing,
soon.

00:09:49.234 --> 00:09:51.534
But as I said earlier this week,
people --

00:09:51.534 --> 00:09:54.067
And by the way, my Corvette
is in a locked garage.

00:09:54.067 --> 00:09:56.400
Okay? So it's not like you're
sitting out in the street.

00:09:56.400 --> 00:09:59.567
But as I said earlier this week,
people know

00:09:59.567 --> 00:10:03.634
I take classified documents and
classified material seriously.

00:10:03.634 --> 00:10:05.968
I also said
we're cooperating fully

00:10:05.968 --> 00:10:08.434
and completely with the
Justice Department's review.

00:10:08.434 --> 00:10:09.834
-But why were the documents

00:10:09.834 --> 00:10:11.601
specifically
next to the Corvette?

00:10:11.601 --> 00:10:14.767
Does he think reading documents
make you look like a nerd,

00:10:14.767 --> 00:10:16.968
so he wanted something kick-ass
next to them?

00:10:16.968 --> 00:10:19.067
"Mr. President, we have
intelligence on North Korea

00:10:19.067 --> 00:10:20.200
you need to read ASAP."

00:10:20.200 --> 00:10:21.701
"Aw, my Corvette's too far away.

00:10:21.701 --> 00:10:23.701
Get me my Ray-Bans
and my Harley jacket."

00:10:23.701 --> 00:10:24.868
[ Laughter ]

00:10:24.868 --> 00:10:26.267
House Republicans are trying
to go after Biden

00:10:26.267 --> 00:10:28.000
and protect Trump,
but the two situations

00:10:28.000 --> 00:10:30.033
are in no way comparable.
Trump is under multiple

00:10:30.033 --> 00:10:31.767
criminal investigations
for many things,

00:10:31.767 --> 00:10:33.601
from his family business
to his coup attempt

00:10:33.601 --> 00:10:35.634
to his refusal to hand over
classified documents.

00:10:35.634 --> 00:10:37.534
Biden is at least cooperating.

00:10:37.534 --> 00:10:39.501
When the Feds
showed up at Mar-a-Lago,

00:10:39.501 --> 00:10:42.100
Trump didn't exactly run to the
door like this.

00:10:42.100 --> 00:10:44.634
[ Laughter ]

00:10:44.634 --> 00:10:46.467
This has been "A Closer Look."

00:10:46.467 --> 00:10:48.467
[ Theme music plays ]

00:10:48.467 --> 00:10:50.467
[ Cheers and applause ]

